Implemented the mushroom jump pad behavior.

Changed:
- `player/player.gd`
  - Added `launch_from_jump_pad(launch_velocity)` to replace the player’s velocity with a deterministic launch vector and trigger jump animation state.

- `jumping_pad/jumping_pad.gd`
  - Detects `body_entered` and only reacts to `Player`.
  - Launches along `global_transform.basis.y`, so tilted pads launch along their surface normal.
  - Uses `launch_speed = 32.0`, much stronger than the normal jump.
  - Replaces existing momentum instead of adding to it.
  - Keeps normal player air movement behavior after launch.
  - Adds retriggerable squash/rebound tween animation for the mushroom cap/root.
  - Ignores all non-player bodies.

Verified:
- Started `res://main.tscn` through the Godot MCP runner.
- No script/parser/runtime errors reported.
- Stopped the project cleanly afterward.

Note: the worktree already had unrelated untracked config files: `.claude/`, `.gemini/`, `.mcp.json`, `opencode.json`. I did not touch them.
